from urllib.parse import urlencode

# Focused buying and service intent, with no invented stock, specifications or response promises.
PARTS=[
('flag-clips-snap-hooks','Flag clips & snap hooks','Small connections.<br>Keep the flag attached.','Match replacement clips to your flag, halyard and existing pole arrangement.','accessories','Stainless steel snap hooks, a coil of halyard rope and aluminum flagpole accessories',
 'A missing or worn clip can leave a flag hanging unevenly or prevent a straightforward replacement. A useful parts request starts with a photograph of the existing connection and the flag’s attachment points.',
 [('Connection style','Show how the existing clip connects to the rope and to the flag. Swivel clips, fixed hooks and other fasteners are not automatically interchangeable.'),('Opening and fit','Include measurements only when the part is safely accessible. The clip must suit the flag attachment as well as the rope or assembly.'),('Operating environment','Describe outdoor exposure and the pole material. Ask about suitable material and any protective cover needed for the arrangement.')],
 'Send photos of the existing clip, flag attachment and rope; quantity needed; and any manufacturer information. Do not detach an overhead or tensioned component to identify it.',
 ('Can I order a clip just from a photograph?','A photograph is a useful start. Dimensions or product details may still be needed before a compatible replacement can be identified.'),'/flagpole-hardware-repair/'),
('halyard-rope','Flagpole halyard rope','The line behind<br>a working display.','Request a compatible replacement rope for an external or internal halyard system.','accessories','White braided rope arranged with metal flagpole hardware',
 'Halyard is the rope used to raise and lower a flag. Rope selection depends on the existing mechanism, attachment arrangement and product requirements—not only on how tall the pole looks.',
 [('System type','Identify an external rope and cleat, or an internal mechanism with an access door. Some systems use cable and require a different replacement approach.'),('Existing specification','Share the manufacturer, rope diameter or previous order record if available. Do not assume a household rope is suitable.'),('Condition of the mechanism','A worn pulley or sharp contact point can damage a new rope. Explain any jamming, fraying or abnormal operation as part of the request.')],
 'Include the pole model if known, approximate height, rope condition and safely taken ground-level photos. Supply-only rope and an installed replacement are different scopes.',
 ('Can a broken rope be replaced without access equipment?','It depends on the pole system and the condition of the remaining line. A lost halyard may require professional access; do not climb or improvise a retrieval method.'),'/flagpole-rope-replacement/'),
('flagpole-cleats','Flagpole cleats','A secure place<br>for the halyard.','Identify a replacement cleat around the pole, mounting arrangement and existing rope system.','hardware','An aluminum flagpole cleat with a neatly secured halyard',
 'The cleat is the fitting used to secure an external halyard. A loose, damaged or unsuitable cleat needs review together with its attachment to the pole.',
 [('Existing mounting','Photograph the fitting and mounting points from a safe position. Hole spacing and attachment details affect compatibility.'),('Rope arrangement','Share the rope size if known and describe how the pole is operated. The cleat needs to suit the intended system.'),('Pole condition','Mention movement, damaged fixings or visible deterioration around the fitting. Replacing the cleat alone may not resolve the underlying issue.')],
 'Send a close photograph only if the fitting is accessible from the ground. Include the pole material, cleat dimensions if safely measurable and whether installation is requested.',
 ('Can new holes be drilled to fit any cleat?','Do not assume this is appropriate. Pole condition, product guidance and the mounting method must be reviewed before changing fixings.'),'/flagpole-hardware-repair/'),
('ball-finials','Flagpole ball finials','Finish the top<br>of the display.','Discuss a replacement ball finial with the size, connection and pole assembly considered.','accessories','Brushed aluminum ball finial beside other flagpole fittings',
 'A ball finial is the ornament at the top of many flagpoles. A matching appearance is only part of the selection: the connection to the pole-top assembly matters too.',
 [('Connection details','Provide a model number or existing product record where possible. Threads and mounting arrangements vary between products.'),('Display proportions','Share the approximate pole height and existing finial size if documented. Final selection should suit the chosen pole assembly.'),('Access and replacement','A missing or damaged finial may involve work at height. Include access constraints and whether the whole top assembly needs review.')],
 'Share ground-level photos, manufacturer information and any records of the original finial. Do not attempt to remove a top fitting to obtain a measurement.',
 ('Does a new finial include a new pulley assembly?','Not necessarily. The ornament and the truck or pulley assembly can be separate components. The quote should identify exactly what is included.'),'/services/pulley-replacement/'),
('wall-brackets','Flagpole wall brackets','Make the connection<br>fit the building.','Explore bracket options for a building-mounted flag display, subject to the wall and fixing requirements.','bracket','Metal flagpole bracket supporting an angled pole at a stone building entrance',
 'A wall bracket connects a pole to a building. The right choice depends on the pole, projection, wall construction and fixing design rather than appearance alone.',
 [('Pole compatibility','Identify the pole diameter and bracket configuration from product information. Send photos when replacing an existing fitting.'),('Building and placement','State the wall material, proposed position and any projection over a path or public area. Include landlord or property approvals.'),('Installation requirements','Fixing suitability cannot be established from an image alone. Any assessment or specialist work needed should be included in the agreed scope.')],
 'Include photographs of the wall and intended display position, pole information and whether a bracket is being replaced or fitted for the first time.',
 ('Can a bracket be fitted to any wall?','No universal assumption should be made. The building, fixing substrate, selected product and display conditions must be considered together.'),'/flagpoles/wall-mounted/'),
('indoor-flag-stands','Indoor flag stands & bases','Give your indoor<br>display a place.','Plan freestanding flags for reception areas, meeting rooms, ceremonies and conference stages.','indoor-display','Two navy and white indoor flags on silver poles with circular floor bases',
 'Indoor stands bring a flag display into a room without a permanent ground installation. Select the pole, flag and base as a compatible arrangement with enough space around it.',
 [('Pole and base fit','Confirm the pole diameter, base connection and product compatibility. A visually similar base may not fit the same pole.'),('Room layout','Include ceiling height, the display footprint and nearby doors, seating or circulation routes.'),('Transport and use','Say whether the display stays in one place or travels between events. Storage and handling needs can affect the choice.')],
 'Send the number of flags, room or stage photos, approximate ceiling clearance and any existing pole information. Mention purchase versus short-term rental.',
 ('Can an indoor floor stand be used outdoors?','Do not assume so. Outdoor exposure, surface and stability requirements are different. Request a system intended for the actual environment.'),'/flag-rentals/corporate-events/')]
MICROS=[
('stuck-flag','Stuck flag & jammed halyard','When the flag<br>won’t move.','Describe a flag that will not raise or lower so the operating system and access needs can be assessed.','hardware','Flagpole rope secured around an aluminum cleat',
 'A stuck flag can involve the rope, clips, pulley or internal operating mechanism. The visible symptom helps define the first assessment; it does not establish the cause on its own.',
 [('What happens','Explain whether the line moves at all, whether the problem is intermittent, and whether anything changed before the issue began.'),('Where it stops','Describe the flag’s position from the ground and whether the rope appears tangled or caught. Photos can help without approaching the equipment.'),('Safe next step','Stop forcing the mechanism. Mention any loose components, unusual pole movement or restrictions around the display.')],
 'Include approximate pole height, internal or external halyard, the current flag position and safe ground-level images. Access requirements are confirmed after review.',
 ('Should I pull harder to free the flag?','No. Forcing a jammed system can worsen damage or create a falling-object hazard. Leave the mechanism alone and request an assessment.'),'/flagpole-repair/'),
('noisy-flagpole','Flagpole noise assessment','Find the source<br>of the clatter.','Request a review of recurring rope or hardware noise around an occupied property.','inspection','Ground-level flagpole hardware being documented beside landscaped grounds',
 'Repeated contact between rope, fittings and the pole can be disruptive near rooms, entrances or shared outdoor space. Describe when the sound occurs so the relevant components can be reviewed.',
 [('Pattern of the sound','Note whether the sound changes with wind, happens during operation or continues while the flag is still.'),('Nearby use','Identify adjacent rooms, guest areas or residences and useful access windows for an inspection.'),('Existing hardware','Share the halyard type, clips and any protective components already fitted. Noise-reduction options depend on compatibility.')],
 'A short description or recording made from a safe position, ground-level photographs and the pole details can help. Avoid tightening, restraining or modifying components without suitable guidance.',
 ('Can the noise be eliminated completely?','No result should be assumed before the cause is assessed. Options depend on the pole system and site conditions, and an outdoor display can still make sound.'),'/flagpole-maintenance/'),
('pulley-replacement','Flagpole pulley & truck replacement','Restore the part<br>that guides the line.','Discuss worn or damaged pole-top hardware and the access required for a compatible replacement.','accessories','Flagpole rope and metal components arranged on a light surface',
 'The truck is the assembly at the top of many flagpoles that supports the pulley and related fittings. Rope wear or difficult operation may justify reviewing this assembly alongside the halyard.',
 [('Assembly identification','Provide the manufacturer or product record if known. Fixed and revolving systems and their mounting arrangements differ.'),('Symptoms and condition','Explain rope wear, jamming or visible damage without assuming which part has failed.'),('Access planning','Include the pole height, surrounding structures, parking restrictions and space available for service equipment.')],
 'Send ground-level images and existing product documentation. The replacement scope may include associated rope or fittings if they are incompatible or damaged.',
 ('Is every pulley compatible with every pole?','No. The assembly, rope arrangement and mounting details need to match the pole system. A replacement is selected after those details are reviewed.'),'/flagpole-rope-replacement/'),
('storm-damage','Post-storm flagpole assessment','After the weather.<br>Before the next flag.','Request a review of visible flag, rope or hardware damage following severe weather.','inspection','Ground-level visual review of a flagpole and secured halyard',
 'A torn flag, loose fitting or change in the appearance of a pole is a reason to assess the display before normal use resumes. Describe observations; do not attempt a test that could create further risk.',
 [('What changed','Note torn fabric, a loose line, visible movement or components on the ground. Include the approximate date of the weather event.'),('Condition of the area','Keep people away from visibly unstable equipment or loose overhead parts and follow your property’s incident procedures.'),('Assessment scope','A routine visual review is different from an engineering assessment. The appropriate next step depends on the reported condition.')],
 'Provide the site address, safe distant photos, approximate height and any access restrictions. If there is immediate danger, use the appropriate local emergency channel; this quote form is not an emergency dispatch service.',
 ('Can a damaged flag simply be replaced?','Sometimes the flag is the only affected item, but that should not be assumed when the pole or hardware also shows signs of damage. Identify those concerns before requesting a routine flag change.'),'/flagpole-inspection/'),
('seasonal-flag-change','Seasonal flag change service','A fresh display.<br>A planned visit.','Coordinate a scheduled flag change around your property’s calendar, access and approved designs.','hero','Flags flying beside a landscaped commercial property',
 'A seasonal change can align flags with a property schedule, event or planned replacement cycle. A clear brief identifies what comes down, what goes up and how the old flags should be handled.',
 [('Flag schedule','List the approved designs, dimensions, quantities and intended change dates for each display.'),('Site access','Identify the property contact and any work windows, locks or access procedures that affect the visit.'),('Replacement details','State whether flags are supplied by you or requested with the service. Agree handling of removed flags rather than assuming disposal or storage.')],
 'Send the current display details, replacement artwork or flag list and preferred dates. Timing, product availability and included tasks are confirmed in the quote.',
 ('Can the same schedule cover several properties?','A multi-location request can list each site’s dates, contacts and flag requirements. Service arrangements are assessed separately for the locations involved.'),'/flag-service/'),
('event-setup-takedown','Event flag setup & takedown','Arrive ready.<br>Leave the venue clear.','Request a coordinated flag display setup and removal plan for your event venue.','indoor-display','Freestanding navy and white flags arranged in a conference reception',
 'Setup and takedown have their own timing and access requirements. Include both in the brief so the display can be planned around deliveries, rehearsals, public opening and venue handback.',
 [('Display plan','List flag designs, quantities, poles and bases, and provide a layout showing the intended positions.'),('Two access windows','Give the setup and collection times, including loading arrangements and the on-site contact for each.'),('Venue conditions','Describe surfaces, indoor or outdoor use, circulation routes and the venue’s temporary-display requirements.')],
 'Include the event schedule, venue plan, display list and any permissions needed for placement. Installation, rental products and transport should each be identified in the agreed scope.',
 ('Does renting flags automatically include setup and collection?','No. Request each service you need. Availability, access, staffing and timing are confirmed in the rental or service proposal.'),'/flag-rentals/')]

def focused_page(record,ispart):
 slug,title,headline,desc,image,alt,intro,sections,brief,answer,related=record
 path=('/accessories/' if ispart else '/services/')+slug+'/'
 need='Other' if ispart else ('Flag Rental' if slug=='event-setup-takedown' else 'Flag Replacement' if slug=='seasonal-flag-change' else 'Flagpole Repair')
 quote='/quote/?'+urlencode({'need':need,'topic':title})
 body=hero('PARTS & ACCESSORIES' if ispart else 'SPECIALIST FLAG SERVICE',headline,desc,image,alt)
 body=body.replace('href="/quote/"',f'href="{esc(quote)}"',1)
 body+='<section class="wrap micro-intro"><p class="eyebrow">'+('COMPATIBILITY COMES FIRST' if ispart else 'START WITH THE RIGHT DETAILS')+'</p><p class="large-copy">'+intro+'</p></section>'
 body+='<section class="wrap micro-details">'+''.join(f'<article><span class="micro-number">{i+1:02d}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></article>' for i,(title,text) in enumerate(sections))+'</section>'
 body+='<section class="content-band"><div class="wrap two-column"><div>'+section_head('MAKE YOUR REQUEST USEFUL','A better brief.<br>A clearer quote.')+'</div><div><p>'+brief+'</p><p>'+('Product options, compatibility, stock and lead times are confirmed for your request.' if ispart else 'Service availability, equipment access and the final scope depend on the location and reported conditions.')+'</p>'+link(quote,'REQUEST A PARTS QUOTE' if ispart else 'REQUEST SERVICE','button')+'</div></div></section>'
 body+=faq([answer,('What if I do not know the model or dimensions?','Send the information you have, including existing records and photos taken from a safe position. Do not climb, dismantle or alter the display to complete the enquiry.')])
 related_title=next((p['title'] for u,p in PAGES.items() if u==related),'Related flagpole service')
 body+='<section class="wrap section">'+section_head('COMPLETE THE REQUEST','Related solutions.')+cards([(related_title,related,'Review the connected product or service requirements.'),('Parts & accessories','/accessories/','Identify components before choosing replacements.'),('Commercial flag management','/flag-service/','Coordinate care across the seasons or multiple sites.')])+'</section>'
 add(path,title,desc,body)
 return (title,path,desc,image,alt)
part_cards=[focused_page(x,True) for x in PARTS]
service_cards=[focused_page(x,False) for x in MICROS]
def illustrated_cards(items):
 return '<div class="illustrated-grid">'+''.join(f'<a class="illustrated-card" href="{u}">{img(im,alt)}<div><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p><span class="text-link">EXPLORE</span></div></a>' for t,u,d,im,alt in items)+'</div>'
add('/accessories/','Flagpole parts & accessories','Explore clips, halyards, cleats, finials, wall brackets and indoor stands. Request parts around the existing system and display.',hero('PARTS & ACCESSORIES','The details behind<br>a better display.','From the clip on your flag to the base beneath a stand, identify the right component before arranging a replacement.','accessories','Flagpole clips, rope, cleat and ball finial on a light work surface')+'<section class="wrap section">'+section_head('FIND THE PART','What needs attention?','Compare the details that matter. Product options and compatibility are confirmed in your quote.')+illustrated_cards(part_cards)+'</section>')
add('/services/specialist/','Specialist flagpole & display services','Find focused guidance for jammed flags, noise, pulley replacement, storm damage, seasonal changes and event setup.',hero('SPECIALIST SERVICES','One specific problem.<br>A considered next step.','Tell us what has changed or what you need arranged. Start with the situation that best describes your request.','inspection','A ground-level review of flagpole rope and hardware')+'<section class="wrap section">'+illustrated_cards(service_cards)+'</section>')
PAGES['/services/']['body']+='<section class="wrap section">'+section_head('LOOKING FOR SOMETHING SPECIFIC?','Find your next step.')+illustrated_cards(service_cards)+'</section>'
PAGES['/flagpoles/']['body']+='<section class="wrap section">'+section_head('COMPLETE THE SYSTEM','Parts that fit the display.')+illustrated_cards(part_cards[:3])+link('/accessories/','ALL PARTS & ACCESSORIES','button navy')+'</section>'
PAGES['/']['body']+='<section class="wrap section"><div class="section-title-row">'+section_head('THE SMALL THINGS MATTER','Parts. Care.<br>A complete display.')+link('/accessories/','EXPLORE ACCESSORIES','text-link')+'</div>'+illustrated_cards([part_cards[0],part_cards[5],service_cards[1]])+'</section>'
# Route-specific links beside existing relevant services.
for path,subset in [('/flagpole-hardware-repair/',part_cards[:5]),('/flagpole-repair/',service_cards[:4]),('/flag-rentals/',[part_cards[5],service_cards[5]])]:
 PAGES[path]['body']+='<section class="wrap section">'+section_head('LOOK CLOSER','More specific options.')+cards([(t,u,d) for t,u,d,im,alt in subset])+'</section>'
